# Product Copy & UI Layout

## Copywriting

- Write for a non-technical user. Never put infrastructure jargon in the UI (`cron`, IMAP internals, OAuth, webhook, bearer token, etc.) unless the screen is explicitly for developers.
- Prefer plain outcomes: “checks for new emails every 5 minutes”, not “server cron”.
- Keep supporting sentences short. One idea per line under a heading.
- Apply the humanizer skill for narrative UI copy: no promotional filler, no AI vocabulary.

## Toolbar / filter layouts

- Keep related controls in **one horizontal group** on desktop (filter + primary action). Do not wrap the primary action under only part of the filter cluster.
- Align controls on a shared baseline (`items-end` or equal-height inputs).
- On small screens, stack as: filters row, then full-width action — not a broken L-shape.
- Prefer a single `month` control (e.g. `<input type="month">`) over separate month + year fields when both only select a period.

## When claiming UI/copy done

Show a fresh screenshot of the affected screen in the same reply.
